    "title": "School district begins new year - NewsBreak",
    "text": "MARATHON — Monroe County Schools Superintendent Ed Tierney welcomed the district leadership team to the annual district retreat in early August to formally start the back to school activities. More than 50 district leaders gathered in the Emergency Operations Center in Marathon to celebrate the district’s A grade (the state’s highest grade) and plan for the upcoming school year. “Rigor is the new norm” is the theme for teachers, students and parents this school year. The goal is to teach using the highest standards and support students and teachers in reaching success, Tierney said. The retreat was an opportunity for team members to get to know each other, discuss their roles within the district and assess progress within the strategic plan. Tierney and district staff seek to lead personnel in increasing performance in safety, academics and students’ overall well-being and access to wider opportunities. Partnership with families and the community is considered integral and the district aims to continuously share information via text and call messages, Facebook, Instagram and on its website, keysschools.com. Teachers reported to school Wednesday, Aug. 6, and the first day of school for students was a week later.",
